# Security Guidelines

## Framework Security Classes
The framework provides comprehensive security classes in [Brain/Classes/security/](mdc:Brain/Classes/security/):

### Core Security Components
- [Brain/Classes/security/Acl.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/security/Acl.php) - Access Control Lists
- [Brain/Classes/security/Auth.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/security/Auth.php) - Authentication system
- [Brain/Classes/security/Csrf.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/security/Csrf.php) - CSRF protection
- [Brain/Classes/security/encryption.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/security/encryption.php) - Data encryption
- [Brain/Classes/security/Firewall.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/security/Firewall.php) - Application firewall
- [Brain/Classes/security/Validator.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/security/Validator.php) - Input validation
- [Brain/Classes/security/Sanitizer.php](mdc:Brain/Classes/security/Sanitizer.php) - Data sanitization

## Authentication & Authorization

### User Authentication
- Use the Auth class for user authentication
- Implement proper session management
- Use secure password hashing (PHP's `password_hash()`)
- Implement account lockout mechanisms
- Use multi-factor authentication where appropriate

### Access Control
- Implement Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
- Use the Acl class for permission management
- Validate permissions on every request
- Implement proper session timeout
- Use secure session configuration

## Input Validation & Sanitization

### Data Validation
- Always validate user input using the Validator class
- Implement both client-side and server-side validation
- Use appropriate validation rules for different data types
- Validate file uploads thoroughly
- Implement input length limits

### Data Sanitization
- Use the Sanitizer class for data cleaning
- Escape output in views to prevent XSS
- Use prepared statements for database queries
- Sanitize file names and paths
- Validate and sanitize JSON input

## CSRF Protection
- Use the Csrf class for form protection
- Include CSRF tokens in all forms
- Validate CSRF tokens on form submission
- Implement proper token rotation
- Use SameSite cookies for additional protection

## Data Encryption
- Use the encryption class for sensitive data
- Encrypt passwords and sensitive information
- Use proper encryption algorithms
- Implement key rotation policies
- Secure encryption key storage

## Security Headers
- Implement proper HTTP security headers
- Use Content Security Policy (CSP)
- Set X-Frame-Options header
- Implement X-XSS-Protection
- Use Strict-Transport-Security for HTTPS

## File Upload Security
- Validate file types and sizes
- Scan uploaded files for malware
- Store uploaded files outside web root
- Use secure file naming conventions
- Implement file access controls

## API Security
- Implement proper API authentication
- Use rate limiting for API endpoints
- Validate API requests thoroughly
- Implement proper error handling
- Log API access and errors

## Security Monitoring
- Implement security logging
- Monitor for suspicious activities
- Use the framework's audit trail features
- Implement intrusion detection
- Regular security assessments